Research decision memo — Stage 8
Title: New Keynesian Integration after General-Equilibrium Compatibility
Status: NOT STARTED

Central hypothesis: Which equilibrium-compatible statistical-mechanical mechanisms add distinct predictions for inflation, monetary transmission, wealth inequality and welfare once nominal rigidity is introduced?

Feasibility prior:
Proceed only after mechanisms in Stages 2–7 have individually passed feasibility, rational-expectations and market-clearing checks.

Core economic distinction:
Standard NK and HANK benchmark without statistical-mechanical components

Conditions to check:
1. Firm dynamic optimal pricing and Calvo price index
2. Household Euler/Bellman equations with rational equilibrium forecasts
3. Goods, labor, money/bonds and security-market clearing
4. Central bank policy rule and equilibrium transition

Pass / fail criterion:
Do not implement before Stages 0–4 pass their core gates; optional firm/finance modules enter only if Stages 5–7 pass.

The project reports negative feasibility results when a kinetic, entropy, adaptive-trading, or heuristic-firm mechanism cannot be reconciled with optimization and equilibrium. Do not silently weaken rational expectations or drop clearing equations.

Evidence status: no derived theorems, numerical solutions or validated simulations committed yet.
